      "id": 1,
      "text": "Joshua was named after the biblical figure, platted in 1880, and organized in 1881 when the Gulf, Colorado and Santa Fe Railroad arrived.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.johnsoncountytx.org/departments/museum/joshua"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Joshua sits at the junction of State Highway 174 and Farm Road 917, on the historic Atchison, Topeka and Santa Fe line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/joshua-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s name was chosen by Dr. McMillan, who honored the biblical Joshua in the early 1880s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/joshua-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Joshua lies within Texas’s Cross Timbers, a forested prairie that stretches across the state’s north-central region.",
